# Trivy accepted-exception list (DRRA finding 9 — documented exception process).
#
# ENFORCEMENT: BLOCKING. The "Vulnerability policy" CI step fails the build on
# FIXED Critical/High findings in the repository dependency manifests that are
# NOT listed below. Unfixed vulnerabilities never block (ignore-unfixed) until an
# upstream fix exists; they are tracked via the SARIF report in GitHub code
# scanning.
#
# SCOPE: this gate scans the Python dependency manifest (requirements.txt) and
# the Rust crate lockfile (watchers/Cargo.lock) via `trivy fs`. It EXCLUDES the
# frontend lockfile (dashboard/ is skipped) and does NOT cover the built
# container image, OS packages, or runtime-installed libraries — those are
# separate scanners (see CLAIM_TRACEABILITY.md, "Full-stack vuln scanning").
#
# TO ACCEPT AN EXCEPTION, add one CVE id per line (its own line — do not rely on
# inline trailing comments), each with a preceding comment block that records:
#   Justification : why the risk is acceptable / not reachable in our usage
#   Owner         : who accepted it
#   Approved-by   : reviewer who signed off
#   Review-by     : expiration date (YYYY-MM-DD) after which it must be re-checked
#
# Example (commented out — not an active exception):
# Justification: not reachable; the vulnerable codepath is unused in DRRA.
# Owner: Surya Nalluri
# Approved-by: <reviewer>
# Review-by: 2026-12-31
# CVE-0000-00000
#
# --- active exceptions below (none currently) ---
